{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763614, "segment_id": "cKcjG3i53f", "segment_broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Russ Mitchell (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763614, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763614, "segment_id": "uhCUV0vjZC", "segment_broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "segment_title": "New York, New York / Convention Security", "segment_description": "(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  Report introduced. \n (New York: Jim Axelrod)  Security in New York City for the Republican National Convention featured; scenes shown of abortion rights protesters & last night's protest by bicyclists.  [NYC police commissioner Raymond KELLY, bike PROTESTER, NEW YORKER&nbsp- comment.] \n (New York: Serena Altschul)  The planned protests previewed.  [San Francisco DEMONSTRATOR, protestor Veronia GIMENEZ&#134;- outline their goal.]  [American University James THURBER&#134;- explains how protests could help President Bush.]", "segment_duration": 230, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763615, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763614, "segment_id": "qoAR3ClYnK", "segment_broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "segment_title": "Campaign 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Kerry Military Record", "segment_description": "(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  Report introduced. \n (Ohio: Mark Knoller)  President Bush's campaign swing through battleground states before the Republican National Convention featured; scenes shown from Ohio.  [In Troy & Lima, BUSH\u00a0- campaigns.] \n (Studio: Russ Mitchell)  May 27 speech from former Democratic Texas Lt. Gov. Ben Barnes\u2020 about how he helped get George Bush into the Texas National Guard recalled.  [BARNES\u00a0- says he got Bush into the guard.] \n (Seattle: Byron Pitts)  Senator John Kerry's campaign on the defense after the ad campaign against his Vietnam war service record featured; scenes shown from today's rally in Washington state.  [KERRY, Senator John EDWARDS\u00a0- campaign.]  [Kerry supporters Sarah GONZALES\u2020, Kathy DEWOSKIN\u2020- offer views.]  [June 4, wife Teresa HEINZ KERRY\u00a0- says John is cool under fire.]", "segment_duration": 230, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63270.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763616, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763614, "segment_id": "iA6XiT2HNz", "segment_broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "segment_title": "Afghanistan / War", "segment_description": "(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  The coalition's killing in Afghanistan of a major Taliban leader linked to Al Qaeda reported.   ( Afghanistan: Lara Logan)  Phone report on the Taliban raid presented.", "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63500.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763617, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763614, "segment_id": "KJRIDW0eZu", "segment_broadcast_id": "sm8n4aeyK9", "segment_title": "US-Israeli Relations / Espionage / Pentagon Spy", "segment_description": "(Studio: Russ Mitchell)  Report introduced.   (Studio: Randall Pinkston)  The FBI investigation into spying for Israel by a Pentagon analyst working for Undersecretary of Defense Douglas Feith&#134; reviewed; details given about the espionage investigation into the passing of classified information to the American Israel Public Affairs Committee {AIPAC} & on to Israel.  The 1985 arrest of Jonathan Pollard for passing documents to Israel recalled.  [Hebrew University Martin VAN CREVELD&#134;- doubts Israel would take the risk.]", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63560.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763618, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadca